>>
Rule 1 (tensor input must be 2D or 3D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 3
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (tensor input must have valid dimensionality)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= -1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 4 (tensor should not contain zero dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ 0
